        {
          "ruleId": "ai-slop-desktop-windows-open-diverges",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Share one implementation (the quoted raw_arg /select form and the rundll32 url.dll,FileProtocolHandler command) between the two hosts, or port both fixes and their tests into services.rs.: The Tauri desktop host re-implements open_url/reveal for Windows without the fixes the egui app already carries for the same OS calls. services.rs open_url runs `explorer <url>`, which apps/lightcraft/src/main.rs documents (issue #234) as opening File Explorer instead of the browser for links with a query or fragment (e.g. an OpenStreetMap map link). services.rs reveal passes `format!(\"/select,{path}\")` through Rust's arg quoting, which the same file documents (issue #272) as making Explorer open Documents instead of selecting the file whenever the path contains a space, and it does not strip the `\\\\?\\` verbatim prefix. On Windows, Reveal in Explorer on `C:\\My Photos\\a.jpg` or opening a link with `?`/`#` from the desktop app misbehaves; the egui app has regression tests for exactly these cases, the desktop host has none."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/lightcraft-desktop/src/services.rs"
                },
                "region": {
