          "ruleId": "arch-duplicate-preferences-patch-paths-diverge",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Route lc_native preferences.patch through the same helper as lc_preferences and decide once whether a missing host is an error after the preference file has been written.: Preferences are patched through two IPC entry points with copy-pasted bodies that disagree when the desktop host failed to start: lc_preferences writes ui.json via preferences.patch and then returns Err(startup_error), while lc_native action preferences.patch performs the same write and returns Ok(value). The frontend therefore reports a failed save for a write that actually persisted (or a success, depending on which entry point the caller used), and fixes to one path do not reach the other."
