          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Have export_metadata take the resolved removes_location(photo, catalog, o) result (or call it) instead of reading o.remove_location, so one function owns the location decision for all export formats.: removes_location() is the declared seam for location policy ('photo and catalog let library-level privacy rules add to the export option') and the Original/DNG path (prepare_guarded, export.rs:1753-1755) goes through it, but export_metadata() for every rendered format reads o.remove_location directly (export.rs:1597, 1610). The moment a library-level rule is added to removes_location as its doc invites, Original/DNG exports drop GPS while JPEG/TIFF/PSD/WebP/AVIF/JXL exports still embed GPS and place names, leaking the location the rule was meant to strip."
