          "ruleId": "arch-qa-mode-detection-ungated-in-release",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Compute one RuntimeMode once at startup (behind cfg(feature = \"qa-native\") for every env-derived input) and pass it to build_shell, run(), lc_native and the macOS builder branch; release builds should compile the QA branches out.: QA mode is derived in five independent places with different gating. runtime_modes deliberately ignores LIGHTCRAFT_DESKTOP_QA/RIGHTKIT_QA_HIDDEN/RIGHTKIT_QA_BACKGROUND unless the qa-native feature is built (default = [] in Cargo.toml), but unattended_qa_enabled, build_shell, the lc_native import-picker guard and the macOS activation branch read the same variables unconditionally. A release build launched with any of those variables set (e.g. inherited from a developer or CI shell) therefore uses the production library and preferences while build_shell sets show_on_ready(false) and run() sets focus=false, so the main window never appears, and native pickers are rejected as 'unavailable in hidden QA'. This also leaves QA control behaviour compiled into release builds rather than stripped."
