        {
          "ruleId": "correctness-cr3-framing-reference-fit-rounding",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Resize the reference to exactly (w, h) as reference_at does (`resize(reference, w, h, Filter::Box)`) instead of fit().: estimate_cr3_framing fits the reference into the proxy's box with fit(), which keeps the reference's own aspect ratio, then returns None unless the size matches exactly. The comment on reference_at (398-402) records that this fit can round one pixel short (191x128 vs 192x128). When that happens, align_cr3_framing silently returns the unaligned sensor, so the CR3 framing correction is skipped for that file and the colour pairs are taken from misregistered pixels."
          },
          "locations": [
