          "ruleId": "correctness-credits-undated-sort-descending",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Apply the direction only to the date comparison and keep undated entries last, e.g. compare (a.is_empty()).cmp(b.is_empty()) first and reverse only the date part when !ascending; add a descending date test.: compare() orders undated (PR-only) contributors via dated()=(is_empty, date) so they sort after everyone with a date, as the comment at line 159 states. sorted() then applies o.reverse() for descending order, which also reverses that rule: with First/Last commit sorted descending (the ▼ toggle in the About window), every PR-only contributor with an empty date jumps to the top of the list ahead of the newest committers."
