          "ruleId": "correctness-lrcat-undo-merge-uses-capped-history-length",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Capture s.commits() before the import and merge s.commits().wrapping_sub(before) steps (as sync.rs:633-639 does), instead of differencing undo.len().: LRCAT import commits the file additions (import::commit_prepared, one undo step) and then the metadata/album batch (a second step), and merges them by comparing s.undo.len() with undo0 captured at lightroom_job.rs:304. Session::commit drops the oldest entry once the history exceeds 1000 (lib.rs:516-519), so in a session whose undo history is already full (1000 steps from ordinary slider edits) undo.len() stays 1000 after both commits: merge_undo(0) is a no-op. The import is left as two undo steps; one Undo removes the ratings/edits/albums but keeps the added photos, a partial undo of an operation that is supposed to be one step."
