          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "In the done callback (and/or at ImportRun start in import::tick) refuse or defer when app.sync_run, app.lightroom or a non-browse scan is present, reusing busy_synchronizing; add a test that completes an auto-import listing while a sync run is active and asserts no ImportTask is created.: Auto Import checks import/sync_run/lightroom only when it spawns the folder listing (lib.rs:1054-1058). The listing runs on a worker (it may take seconds on a network share); its done callback re-checks only app.import.is_none() before installing an ImportTask, and import::tick starts the worker without checking sync_run or lightroom. If the user confirms Synchronize Folder (sync.rs only refuses when app.import is Some) or starts an LRCAT import (lightroom busy() only refuses when app.import is Some) while the listing is in flight, the auto import then starts alongside it. That violates the module's stated invariant that an import and a Synchronize Folder never run at once because each readies files against the library as it was when it started, so both can add the same file (duplicate catalog records); likewise an auto import can run during a catalog import's commit window."
