          "ruleId": "correctness-remote-stale-pool-gives-up",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Treat an I/O failure on a pooled (reused) connection as a reconnect-and-retry on a fresh connection before counting a failure, or stamp pooled connections and drop them past an idle age below the server timeout. Consider resetting failures after a success.: Remote pools idle connections with no liveness check, while the server drops any connection idle past its 120 s read timeout (remote.rs:192). The engine keeps the loaded model, and so its Remote, for the next photo (denoise.rs `loaded`). If the user denoises a photo, waits more than 2 minutes, and starts another, every pooled connection is dead. Each try_run pops one, gets EOF ('the connection closed'), and counts a failure. With 4 slots, 3 failures reach MAX_FAILURES and the server is given up for the rest of the session: the remote GPU is never used again and the status shows 'given up', although the server is healthy."
