          "ruleId": "correctness-shortcuts-x-crop-double-rotate",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Make exactly one of the two fire entries act in the Crop panel: e.g. at line 509 `continue` without running (letting the crop.rotateAspect entry run), or skip the crop.rotateAspect entry when photo.reject is also in `fire`; add a test asserting X in Crop swaps the crop aspect exactly once and adds one undo step.: photo.reject and crop.rotateAspect are both engine commands declared with shortcut X, so in handle() one X press pushes both ids into `fire` (bindable loop, lines 360-370). With the Crop panel open, the photo.reject entry is redirected to crop.rotateAspect (line 509-511) and the crop.rotateAspect entry is NOT skipped (line 513 only skips it outside Crop), so it falls through to app.run at line 559. Pressing X once runs Rotate Crop twice: the aspect is swapped and swapped back (net no visible change) and two 'Rotate Crop' undo steps are recorded. The existing test library_keys_yield_to_search_and_crop_context only asserts the flag stays None, not that the crop rotated once. (Declarations: crates/engine/src/cmd/library.rs:718 and crates/engine/src/cmd/develop.rs:784, both Some(\"X\").)"
