            "text": "Rewrite the module doc to state the actual boundary (pure encoders plus session-bound export orchestration, file I/O and post-processing), or move write_file/AfterExport/PreparedExport file reads into a separate module so the pure claim holds for what remains.: The module doc claims export is 'Pure (bytes in, bytes out) ... writing the file is the caller's job', but the module reads originals from disk (PreparedExport::run, export.rs:1817), owns the native file writer (write_file/write_file_durable, 1991-2008, creating folders and replacing files), and reserves/drives Apple Photos imports (after_export, 1954-1970). A caller relying on the documented purity (e.g. reusing it in the web build or a sandboxed context) gets filesystem and osascript side effects it was told it would not."
