          "message": {
            "text": "Update the comments in crs.rs and files.rs, docs/xmp-interop.md:138 and docs/gaps.md row 8 to cover database profiles; in crs::to_partial carry LensProfileEnable=0 over when the photo's correction came from the database rather than the file (or record the source of embedded_lens so the mapper can tell).: crs.rs:396-398, files.rs:47-49 ('These are the only \"profile\" corrections Ember applies'), docs/xmp-interop.md:138 and docs/gaps.md:29 ('No lens profile database') all say profile corrections are only the file's own embedded ones. Since lens_profiles::for_raw (lens_profiles.rs:63-71) a lensfun-format database (LIGHTCRAFT_LENSFUN_DIR) also fills Photo.embedded_lens, which turns optics.lens_profile on by default (catalog model.rs:418-420). The XMP mapper's rule, built on the stale premise, ignores LensProfileEnable=0, so with a database configured a Lightroom sidecar/LRCAT edit that had profile corrections off imports with database distortion/vignetting correction on: the geometry and the imported crop no longer match the source edit."
