          "ruleId": "doc-lrcat-existing-photos-preserved-overstated",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Either gate the rating/flag/label/meta/captured ops on update_existing (or on the photo being unedited) to match the contract, or narrow the doc comment, command help and docs/lightroom-catalog-import.md to say only develop edits are preserved.: The import contract says 'Existing edited records are preserved unless explicitly requested' (lightroom_catalog.rs:743) and 'Existing edited photos are preserved unless updateExisting=true' (library.importLightroom, cmd/library.rs:1391). In apply_prepared only develop settings are kept (keep_develop, 864-914); for every photo already in the library it unconditionally emits SetRating, SetFlag, SetLabel, SetMeta (keywords replaced wholesale at 891, XMP metadata merged at 875) and SetCaptured (915-922). Re-importing a catalog with updateExisting=false therefore silently overwrites ratings, picks, labels, keywords, metadata and capture-time corrections the user made in Ember, contrary to the documented default (recoverable only by undoing the whole import step)."
