          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Validate `start` (e.g. 0..=999_999 like export's start_number, via usize::try_from and a range check) and return bad params otherwise.: photo.rename / photo.renamePreview take `start` as any u64 and cast it with `as usize`, with no upper bound. plan_rename_core iterates `(start..).zip(photos)`. With start = 18446744073709551615, RangeFrom::next overflows on the first step. In debug builds that panics: the command fails through the catch_unwind net rather than with a bad-params error. In release builds the sequence wraps to 0, 1, …. On 32-bit wasm, the `as usize` cast also silently truncates the value. This breaks the project's never-crash rule for hostile numeric input."
