            "text": "Stage each download under a per-id name (e.g. `.downloads/<id>/<file_name>` or prefix the id), or refuse to start a download whose staged file name is in use by another running or finished job.: Downloads::start only refuses a second download of the same model id; different models download side by side into one shared staging folder keyed only by spec.file_name. Catalog entries (catalog.json) derive file_name from the URL basename and fall back to `model.onnx`, so two catalog models can share a name and write the same `.downloads/<name>.part`. Concurrently, they corrupt each other's partial file and both fail. If one finishes and the second starts before the next faces.pump, the second fetch reuses or overwrites `<name>`. finish_downloads installs the first id with `verified: true` and its recorded sha (no rehash, face_models.rs:265). That can install the other model's bytes under the first model's manifest, or leave the first job's Done path pointing at a file that is gone."
