          "ruleId": "p0004-resilience-1",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Pass --connect-timeout, --max-time and --retry to curl, download to `<name>.part` and rename after the sha256 matches, and keep going after a failed sample, reporting all failures at the end.: `cargo xtask corpus --download` runs curl with no --connect-timeout/--max-time/--retry, writing straight into the final path. A stalled connection hangs the command indefinitely; a mid-transfer failure leaves a truncated file at `out`. The `?` aborts the whole run, and the next run sees `out.exists()`, skips the download, fails the sha256 check, deletes the file and errors again; only the third run actually re-downloads. One transient network error therefore costs two failed runs, and one bad sample stops every later sample from being fetched."
