          "ruleId": "p0004-security-download-pinning-invariant-drift",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Correct the invariant to say catalog.json entries are user-supplied addresses verified by their declared hash/size (or restrict them to https).: The downloader's stated security invariant says only a model in lightcraft_faces::known::download can be fetched, with the address a pinned constant that is never typed or passed in. download_spec falls back to entries from the user-editable catalog.json, whose `url` is arbitrary. So the app fetches from addresses that are neither built in nor pinned. Integrity still holds via the catalog's required sha256/size, but the documented trust boundary that reviewers and agents rely on is false."
