          "ruleId": "p0004-security-keyword-export-overwrites-originals",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Call `s.check_write_target(path)` before writing (as export.contactSheet does) and write atomically.: keyword.export writes the keyword list with std::fs::write to any caller-supplied `path` (UI, CLI or MCP agent) and never calls Session::check_write_target. The app's stated invariant (originals.rs:1-5) is that files Ember writes for the user never land on a catalogued photo's original or XMP sidecar. Other writers enforce it (image exports via OriginalGuard, export.contactSheet, merge). `keyword.export {path: \"/Photos/IMG_0001.xmp\"}`, or the original raw path, silently truncates and replaces that file with a text keyword list. That destroys the photo's sidecar edits and metadata, or the original itself."
          },
