          "ruleId": "p0004-security-placenames-unpinned-base",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Drop the `base` parameter from release builds (keep it behind cfg(test)/debug for the loopback test server) or pin the GeoNames files by size/hash.: metadata.downloadPlaceNames accepts an undocumented `base` parameter that may be any https:// host (base_allowed only checks the scheme). The fetched files carry no size or SHA-256 pin (`size: None, sha256: None`). They are then written as the gazetteer into `dataset`, which is also a caller-chosen folder. An agent or script driving the command interface can make the app fetch from an arbitrary host and install unverified place data. Reverse geocoding then writes that data into photo metadata (City/State/Country) across the library. This contrasts with the face-model downloader, which pins address, size and hash."
