          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Split run_ui_command by command family (view/panel/dialog/file/app) and add a test that every UI_COMMANDS id resolves to Some(..) in run_ui_command, or move to a typed command enum that carries label, shortcut, handler and enablement together.: UI commands are a string table (UI_COMMANDS, 158 ids) whose behaviour lives in a single ~1,525-line match in run_ui_command, with enabled state in a separate string match (ui_enabled) and checked/live-label state in menubar.rs. Nothing ties the table to the handlers at compile time: an id added to UI_COMMANDS but missed or misspelled in run_ui_command falls through `_ => return None` to the engine and fails as an unknown command at runtime, and menu enablement defaults to `true` for any id ui_enabled does not name. All 158 current ids are handled today (checked), so this is a change-risk/shotgun-surgery finding, not a live break."
