        {
          "ruleId": "p0006-arch-dialog-dispatch-scattered",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Move large inline bodies (Export, KeywordTag, KeywordSet, CaptureTime) into their own functions or modules, like Merge, Import and Settings. Consider gathering per-dialog metadata (title, width, window id, Return-confirms, keeps-open) into one method on Dialog, so adding a variant takes one exhaustive match instead of several partial ones.: Each Dialog variant is defined in state.rs (780-1018), but its behaviour is spread over separate exhaustive or partial matches in dialogs.rs: title (223-265), width (289-293), body (299-1120, inside the 1,143-line show() function), confirm_dialog (1571-1751), return_confirms (1946-1948), window_id (176-182) and keeps_open (1416-1418). Some dialogs delegate their body to their own module (Merge, Import, Settings, Sync, Denoise, Faces). Export instead renders 327 lines inline in one match arm (660-987). The partial matches (return_confirms, window_id, keeps_open, width) fall through silently, so a new dialog that needs Return-to-confirm, its own window id, or a stay-open rule compiles without them. The scattering already shows in the confirm_dialog doc comment, which has drifted onto fmt_gap (1400-1402)."
