          "ruleId": "p0006-correctness-geocode-high-latitude-misses",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Widen the longitude search to ceil(MAX_KM / (111.32 km x cos(lat))) cells (clamped, with wrap) instead of a fixed +-1.: reverse() searches only the 3x3 block of 1-degree cells. One degree of longitude is 111 km x cos(lat), under MAX_KM (50 km) above about 63.3 degrees latitude, where cities15000 does list places (Tromso 69.6N, Murmansk 68.9N, Reykjavik 64.1N, Fairbanks 64.8N). A photo at 69.65N, 18.02E sits in cell 18; a place at 69.65N, 16.95E is about 41 km west, within MAX_KM, but lies in cell 16 (dx = -2) and is never examined, so the lookup returns a farther place in the 3x3 block or nothing."
