          "ruleId": "p0006-correctness-smart-migrate-same-folder-deletes",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Before removing src, skip when src and dst are the same file (compare canonicalized paths or (dev, inode)/file id), and have smart_location compare canonicalized directories rather than PathBuf equality.: migrate(Move) deletes the source when a valid proxy already exists at the destination. The only same-folder guard is the lexical `new_dir == current` PathBuf comparison in smart_location (previews.rs). On macOS/Windows case-insensitive volumes, or via a symlink or a `..` spelling, the user can pick the same folder under another spelling (e.g. `/Users/a/Pictures/smart previews` for `/Users/a/Pictures/Smart Previews`). Then for every proxy dst resolves to the same file as src, is_valid(&dst) is true and std::fs::remove_file(&src) deletes it: every smart preview is lost and counted as 'moved'. Smart previews are the only editable copy while originals are offline, so photos on an unplugged drive become uneditable."
