          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Reject rel values containing ':' or any non-Normal path component (use Path::components and require Component::Normal only), and canonicalize the result and require it to start with the canonical serve dir; optionally validate the Host header.: The `cargo xtask web --serve` static server only rejects `..` components and backslashes. On Windows a request such as `GET /C:/Users/<u>/.ssh/id_rsa` yields rel `C:/Users/...`; Path::join with a path carrying a drive prefix replaces the base, so dir.join(rel) reads any file on disk and returns it with 200. The server binds 127.0.0.1 but performs no Host validation, so any local process, or a remote page via DNS rebinding, can read arbitrary developer files while the dev server runs."
