          "ruleId": "perf-snapshot-poll-context-churn",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Skip setSnapshot when the new snapshot is structurally unchanged (compare a host-supplied revision/generation or a cheap hash), split rapidly changing status (jobs/progress) into its own context or selector so grid/inspector consumers do not subscribe to it, and drop JobDialog's separate interval in favour of the provider's single poll.: DesktopProvider polls getSnapshot every 1200 ms (250 ms while importing/exporting/jobs) and calls setSnapshot(next) unconditionally. The IPC result is always a fresh object, so the single memoized context value (snapshot, ui, dialog, error, ...) changes on every poll and every useDesktop() consumer re-renders even when nothing changed. During a long import/export the cadence is 4 Hz, and JobDialog adds its own 300 ms setInterval that also calls refresh(), so the whole shell re-renders and the host session owner serves a full snapshot several times a second while the user is trying to keep working."
