          "ruleId": "res-dns-resolve-ignores-cancel-and-deadline",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Resolve on a helper thread and wait on a channel with the connect timeout, cancel and deadline checks, or document the exception.: Stream::connect resolves the host with to_socket_addrs(), a blocking getaddrinfo call that honours neither the cancel flag, the connect timeout, nor the whole-operation deadline (limits.check() runs only before and after). With a broken resolver or captive network the worker thread blocks for the OS resolver timeout (often tens of seconds) after the user cancels a download or after the 20/45 s deadline of an OpenRouter request, contradicting the module's stated guarantee that a dead server or cancelled download never hangs the thread. Quit-time task waits are held up as well."
