            "text": "Add a timeout to the snapshot IPC (reject after a few seconds, clear refreshInFlight in finally as now, and surface the error), and make the host-side recv bounded; do not make command completion wait on the shared in-flight promise.: refresh() deduplicates through refreshInFlight and returns the stored promise to every caller, and run() awaits refresh() after almost every command. getSnapshot() reaches host.snapshot(), which waits for the session owner with an unbounded recv(). If the owner is wedged (or the snapshot never replies), the in-flight promise never settles, refreshInFlight stays set forever, every later poll and every command awaiting refresh() hangs on the same pending promise, and no error is ever surfaced because neither .then nor .catch runs: the UI stops updating and every menu action appears to do nothing, with no recovery short of restarting."
