          "ruleId": "resil-remote-denoise-permanent-giveup",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "On an I/O failure of a pooled connection, retry once on a fresh connection before counting a failure, and make the failure count consecutive (reset on success) or time-decayed.: `Remote` keeps pooled TCP connections open and the server closes idle connections after its 120 s timeout. `run_now` pops a pooled connection and, when the write or reply fails on a connection the server already closed, returns the error with no retry on a fresh connection. `try_run` adds it to `failures`, a cumulative counter that is never reset on success and has no time decay. After an idle gap or a brief network blip, up to `slots` (4) stale pooled connections each fail one tile. After `MAX_FAILURES` = 3 total failures `healthy()` stays false for the life of the loaded model. The remote GPU is permanently abandoned (\"given up\") for the session although the server is fine, and denoise silently runs on the local runner only."
