          "ruleId": "schema-snapshot-doc-version-drift",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Change the comment to reference VERSION (\"version\":V) as the module docs do.: write_snapshot's contract comment says the catalog.snap bytes are exactly {\"format\":\"lightcraft-catalog\",\"version\":1,...}, but the writer emits version {VERSION} (currently 8). Anyone building a reader or a fixture from this documented byte layout writes version 1, which Journal::open then treats as an older format and rewrites (reported as upgraded_from 1), and a v1-gated external tool would reject real snapshots."
