          "ruleId": "schema-xmp-dc-creator-seq-collapsed",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Keep the creator list structured (e.g. a Vec in Metadata), or split artist on the same \"; \" separator when writing so that read and write are inverses.: dc:creator is an ordered rdf:Seq of creators. parse_xmp joins every entry into one string (\"Alice; Bob\") and write_xmp_lc writes Metadata.artist back as a single rdf:li. Because Ember's sidecar merge owns dc:creator (always replaced on save), a sidecar from another app with creators [Alice, Bob] is rewritten on Ember's next save as one creator \"Alice; Bob\", even when the user never edited the artist. Other readers then see one creator whose name contains a semicolon."
