          "ruleId": "security-cr2-slice-width-overflow",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Sum the widths with checked_add (as sraw.rs does) and reject any slice width greater than the frame's samples per row before slicing.: The CR2 slice tag (CR2_SLICE) values s[1] and s[2] are taken from the file unbounded (only >0 checked) and summed with an unchecked iter().sum(). A crafted CR2 with, e.g., slices [1, 2^63, 2^63+1] makes the sum wrap to width=1 in release, which passes the total%width check. Mode::Full then executes data[y*width+x0 .. +sw] with sw=2^63 and panics (debug builds panic at the sum). Opening the file in the app crashes the decode thread, or aborts the web build (panic=abort). The sibling sRAW path uses try_fold/checked_add (cr2/sraw.rs:87)."
          },
